    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 021915\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1215 PM PDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Above-normal temperatures and quiet conditions continue into \n  next week as high pressure dominates.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Through Thursday\n\nA persistent ridge will be the main driver of weather over the \nsouthwestern United States for the foreseeable future. This pattern \nwill maintain above normal temperatures, with afternoon highs 5 to \n10 degrees above normal for early October. This includes highs in \nthe mid 90s in Las Vegas and the upper 100s in Death Valley. The \nposition of the ridge will direct any atmospheric moisture away from \nthe area, which will keep precipitation out of the forecast. Winds \nwill be light on most days. A weak shortwave may bring breezy \neasterly to southeasterly winds to parts of southern Nevada and \nsoutheastern California on Sunday and knock temperatures down a few \ndegrees on Monday, but the ridge will rebound Tuesday through the \nend of the week. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill remain light and follow typical daily directional patterns \nthrough Saturday. The chance of seeing sustained speeds of 10 \nknots or greater is less than 10 percent, although a random gust \nto 15 knots cannot be ruled out during peak afternoon heating. VFR\nconditions will prevail through Saturday with only a few high \nclouds expected.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Light winds following \ntypical diurnal patterns are expected at regional TAF sites through \nSaturday. Breezy conditions are forecast each afternoon across the \nwestern Mojave Desert and southern Great Basin, but gusts should \nremain 25 knots or less and generally be from a southerly or \neasterly direction. VFR conditions will prevail through Saturday \nwith only a few high clouds expected.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Meltzer\nAVIATION...Planz\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
